From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:34:34 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 49/66] Meridian: Site Control Center, Arc-style menus, one
 welcome on first launch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The URL pill is Arc's: the address on the left, Copy Link and the sliders
  at the end. The sliders open the Site Control Center: Copy Link, Pin,
  Split, Ask AI; the extensions; and for the site, ad and tracker blocking,
  its permissions, zoom and clearing its cookies, over Chromium's own site
  settings. "Secure" opens the page info, "…" all the site's settings.
- The sidebar's right-click menus are the Electron build's again: a header,
  icons, shortcuts, submenus (Move to Space, Colour, Profile) with swatches
  and checks, keyboard navigation, and they stay inside the window. The
  empty sidebar has its own menu.
- First launch: Chromium's first-run window is gone; it came before the
  welcome tour and left two windows, each with the tour.
- The floating sidebar (⌘S) waits a moment before it slides away, so it can
  be reached; it stays while one of its menus is open.
- Mission Control is centred in the window.
- The home page has Archive, Ask AI and Workbench under the search field and
  the "For developers" card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
